# =============================================================================
# Google Calendar + Google Tasks (Settings / Calendar / Tasks → Connect)
# =============================================================================
# One Connect follows the signed-in Summit user (phone, iPad, laptop).
# Disconnect on any device disconnects all. Tokens are NOT localStorage.
#
# Exact Cloud Console setup (do this once):
#
# 1) Open https://console.cloud.google.com/ and pick (or create) a project
# 2) APIs & Services → Library → enable BOTH:
#      • Google Calendar API
#      • Google Tasks API
# 3) APIs & Services → OAuth consent screen
#      • User type: External (or Internal if Workspace)
#      • Add your Google account as a Test user while in Testing
#      • Scopes used by Summit:
#          https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events
#          https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.calendarlist.readonly
#          https://www.googleapis.com/auth/tasks
#          openid  email  profile
# 4) APIs & Services → Credentials → Create credentials → OAuth client ID
#      • Application type: Web application
#
#    Authorized JavaScript origins (exact, no trailing slash):
#      Local:
#        http://localhost:3001
#        http://127.0.0.1:3001
#        http://192.168.0.95:3001
#      Production HTTPS (required for phone / PWA / Safari — not localhost):
#        https://YOUR-APP.vercel.app
#        https://YOUR-CUSTOM-DOMAIN
#      Copy the live hosts from Vercel → Project → Settings → Domains.
#      If you use www and apex, add BOTH.
#
#    Authorized redirect URIs (Calendar + Tasks server OAuth — exact):
#      Local:
#        http://localhost:3001/api/google/calendar/callback
#        http://127.0.0.1:3001/api/google/calendar/callback
#        http://192.168.0.95:3001/api/google/calendar/callback
#      Production HTTPS:
#        https://YOUR-APP.vercel.app/api/google/calendar/callback
#        https://YOUR-CUSTOM-DOMAIN/api/google/calendar/callback
#
#    Login (Supabase Auth) is a DIFFERENT redirect — keep it too:
#        https://fakvxwchxgolvwilaneo.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
#
# 5) Copy Client ID + Client Secret. Set NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL to the HTTPS
#    origin you registered (same string as the origin list, no path).
# 6) Generate token encryption key:  openssl rand -hex 32
#    Put it in GOOGLE_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY (Vercel env too). Never NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# 7) Restart `npm run dev` / redeploy. Sign in to Summit, then Connect once
#    (Calendar, Tasks, or Settings). Allow Calendar + Tasks.
#
# GIS popup is OK on local Chrome only. Production / PWA / Safari use the
# server code flow so the refresh token stays on your Summit user.
#
# Google / Microsoft LOGIN (Supabase → Authentication → Providers):
#   Google: paste the same Client ID + Client Secret. Redirect used by Supabase:
#     https://fakvxwchxgolvwilaneo.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
#   Microsoft: Azure app registration, same Supabase callback URL.
# Phone LOGIN: Authentication → Providers → Phone (needs Twilio SMS).
#
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret
GOOGLE_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=replace-with-openssl-rand-hex-32
# Production HTTPS origin (no trailing slash). Must match Cloud Console.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://YOUR-APP.vercel.app

# Instant Roofer AI (Measurements → Auto-measure). Same name on Vercel.
# Dashboard: https://api-dashboard.instantroofer.com/  (API Keys)
# Paste the key only — no quotes, no Bearer prefix (both are stripped if present).
INSTANT_ROOFER_API_KEY=

# Human Certified webhook — public host only (localhost will not receive it):
#   https://summit-app-kappa.vercel.app/api/instant-roofer/webhook
# Optional matching secret in Instant Roofer dashboard webhook settings:
# INSTANT_ROOFER_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Optional Google Solar fallback (squares/pitch only; no outline) if Instant Roofer
# is configured but returns no roof. Enable "Solar API" in Cloud Console, then:
# GOOGLE_SOLAR_API_KEY=your-solar-api-key
# (or reuse GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY if Solar is enabled on that key)

# Supabase (Project Settings → API)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxx.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-or-publishable-key
#
# Auth (Login) — add these Redirect URLs in Supabase → Authentication → URL Configuration:
#   http://localhost:3001/auth/callback
#   http://127.0.0.1:3001/auth/callback
#   http://192.168.0.95:3001/auth/callback
#   https://YOUR-APP.vercel.app/auth/callback
#   https://YOUR-CUSTOM-DOMAIN/auth/callback
# Site URL: http://localhost:3001 (local) or the HTTPS URL (phones / Vercel)
# After Google / Microsoft OAuth apps exist, enable those providers in
# Authentication → Providers. Apple is deferred.
